<title>UK: Halifax halts daily share tenders.</title>
<headline>Halifax halts daily share tenders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Halifax Plc said on Wednesday it would not hold any more share tenders until further notice.</p>
<p>Halifax, formerly a building society, had organised a number of tenders since its flotation last Monday, when it assumed bank status. The Halifax handed free shares to 7.6 million Britons, many of whom cashed in the stocks immediately.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, Halifax said it received an average price of 757.3p per share when it sold 6.7 million shares in its latest tender.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
